# Image preview in chat

## Required (same turn)

When you **create or update** any **raster image** (PNG, JPG, WebP, GIF) that the user is meant to **see** (diagrams, exported previews, screenshots, assets):

1. In the **same assistant turn** as writing the file, **Read** that image path with the **Read** tool (workspace or absolute path).
2. **Do not** end the reply with only a file path when a visual check matters—the user expects an **inline preview** in chat.

When you use **GenerateImage**, also **Read** the returned file path in that turn so preview is consistent (unless the client already inlined it and you confirm it).

## SVG

After generating or changing an SVG meant for visual review: **export PNG** (e.g. `sharp` in `fresh-project`) and **Read** the PNG in the **same turn**. Do not skip the Read step.

## Other

When the user asks to **preview** an existing image, **Read** it rather than only naming the path.

**Reason:** Path-only replies force the user to hunt files; Read triggers inline display.

## Clickable link (fresh-project / Vite)

When the deliverable lives in **`fresh-project/public/`** and the user runs **`npm run dev`** (default **port 3000**), end the same reply with a **markdown link** they can click, e.g.:

`[Open rotary-draw-actual-layout.png](http://localhost:3000/rotary-draw-actual-layout.png)`

Also mention the index page: **[All bender diagrams](http://localhost:3000/bender-diagrams.html)** when relevant.

## HTML index pages (`fresh-project/public/*.html`)

Asset links to `.png` / `.svg` must use **underlined** `<a>` styling (`text-decoration: underline` + sensible `text-underline-offset`) so filenames read as clickable, not body copy.

If their dev server uses another port, say so once and they can swap the port in the URL.
